<newsitem itemid="215407" id="root" date="1996-11-25" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Firstbus Plc H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Firstbus Plc H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		6.1		    vs 4.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.8		    vs N/A</p>
<p> Pretax		     25.7		   vs 14.2</p>
<p> Turnover		   246.8		  vs 174.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Pretax results exclude exceptional items. After exceptional charges and costs, pretax profit was 23.5 million stg versus 9.0 million stg.</p>
<p>The company said it raised its interim dividend by 12.5 percent versus a year ago.  </p>
<p> Interest payable	 6.8		    vs 4.7</p>
<p> Tax credit		 3.1		    vs 3.0 payable</p>
<p> Net taxed		  26.6		   vs 6.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 19, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Jan 14, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Jan 6, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE: Net taxed results include restructuring and other costs of 2.2 million stg in first half versus about 5.2 million stg in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Firstbus is a local bus operator.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
